Neroth.wikitext:
{{otheruses|USE=character from Dawn of War II|OTHERUSE=antagonist of [[Warhammer 40,000: Space Marine]]|OTHERPAGE=Nemeroth}}
{{BlackLegionPortal}}
[[Image:Neroth.png|thumb|right|Neroth]]
'''Neroth''' is a [[Sorcerer]] of the [[Black Legion]], serving as an agent of [[Ezekyle Abaddon]], the Warmaster of Chaos. He was tasked with accompanying and monitoring [[Eliphas the Inheritor]], to ensure that Eliphas fulfilled his bargain with Abaddon.{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Neroth is a Chaos Sorcerer, wielding the power of the [[Warp]] to summon [[daemon]]s and unleash destructive [[psychic]] attacks. He is characterised by a sadistic glee in violence and destruction, showing more interest in carnage than subtle manipulation. Despite technically following Eliphas’ orders during the campaign, it was made clear that Neroth did so only because it aligned with Abaddon's current will.{{Fn|1}}

His role was primarily that of an enforcer, constantly reminding Eliphas of the consequences of failure. He revels in the madness and destruction wrought by the forces of Chaos.{{Fn|1}}

{{Clear}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*Neroth is a playable hero unit in the Chaos campaign of the video game [[Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War II - Retribution|Dawn of War II – Retribution]].{{Fn|1}}
*Neroth should not be confused with [[Nemeroth]], a separate Chaos Space Marine who appears in [[Warhammer 40,000: Space Marine]].

