Neth.wikitext:
{{NecronsPortal}}
'''Neth''' was a [[Necron]] [[Royal Warden]] of the [[Ithakas Dynasty]].{{Fn|1a}}

The Praetor of [[Sedh]]'s garrison, during the [[Great Sleep]] his cognitive systems were damaged and he has suffered continual mental deterioration. Despite this, he dutifully served his [[Necron Lord|Lord]] [[Oltyx]]. After an [[Ork]] attack on Sedh, an enraged Oltyx was about to execute Neth for his failure. However Oltyx's strategic submind intervened, sparring Neth and giving him a chance to redeem himself.{{Fn|1a}} When Oltyx decided to break his exile and travel to [[Antikef]], he orders Neth not to die as there would be no point in it. Invigorated with newfound enthusiasm, Neth vowed to defend Sedh to the end from any future threats.{{Fn|1c}}

Later, the Ithakas are forced to flee their territories in the face of an [[Imperial]] [[Crusade]]. During the retreat and subsequent battle against the [[Ark Mechanicus]] ''Tyresias'', Neth volunteered to stay behind and hold the line against advancing [[Skitarii]], sacrificing himself in the process.{{Fn|2a}} Oltyx came to regret the loss of Neth and expressed guilt over what had become of him.{{Fn|2b}}

