Nisroc.wikitext:
{{FleshTearersPortal}}
'''Nisroc''' is an [[Apothecary]] in the [[Flesh Tearers]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was among its forces, that took part in the [[Third War of Armageddon]], before the [[Flesh Tearers]] left the warzone. Sometime later, their [[Chapter Master]] [[Gabriel Seth]] led the Flesh Tearers to aid the [[Imperial]] world [[Nekkaris]]. This was after the [[Demagogue]] [[Gylon]] began a [[Chaos Cult]] uprising, with the assistance of the [[Chaos Lord]] [[Da'ka Jumoke]]'s [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]. They had seized Nekkaris' capital and in order to end the rebellion, the Flesh Tearers began advancing upon it with the besieged world's military forces. However before the [[Imperial]]s could reach the capital, the Cult and Warband launched a continuous artillery barrage from armored vehicles, which stopped the advance cold. Even with the Flesh Tearers' might, they would not be able to survive the Chaos forces' rate of fire and so [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Temel]] was selected to lead a group of [[Scout]]s to destroy the artillery in a set time limit. Doing so, would then allow the Imperials to reach the capital and end the rebellion.{{Fn|1}}

As they waited, Nisroc began disparaging [[Nekkaris]]' military aloud for their cowardice, much to the [[Librarian]] [[Balthiel]]'s disappointment. The [[Psyker]] had come to expect such attitudes from [[Chaplain]] [[Appollus]] and the [[Company Champion]] [[Harahel]], but had hoped Nisroc would not do the same. Balthiel noted to himself, however, that the [[Apothecary]] had grown dark, since the Flesh Tearers had fought in the [[Third War of Armageddon]]. The Librarian would tell Nisroc, however, that if he was going to mock Nekkaris' military, the Apothecary should do so privately. After all, the Flesh Tearers would need their aid, once [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Temel]] destroyed the enemy's artillery. While the [[Scouts]] would later succeed in their mission, the Chapter would instead leave Nekkaris in favor of answering a [[Cryptus Campaign|plea for aid]] from the [[Blood Angels]]. The [[Flesh Tearers]]' [[Chapter Master]], [[Gabriel Seth]], felt time was of the essence, so he even refused to wait to evacuate Temel's Scouts and instead regretfully left them to their fates.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
