Noa Vadim.wikitext:
{{TanithPortal}}
'''Noa Vadim''' was a [[Guardsman]] of the [[Tanith First and Only]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
===Verghast===
Vadim was originally a [[Imperial Citizen|citizen]] of [[Vervunhive]] on the planet [[Verghast]]. Prior to the [[Siege of Vervunhive]], he worked as a roofer on the hive's Main Spine, which gave him valuable expertise for working at high altitudes without safety equipment.{{Fn|1a}}

After the Siege of Vervunhive was ended, Vervunhive had been reduced to ruins. [[Warmaster]] [[Macaroth]] allowed any surviving Vervunhiver to [[Act of Consolation|enlist]] with the [[Astra Militarum]] and reinforce one of the regiments fighting in the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]]. Vadim took the offer and was drafted into the Tanith First.{{Fn|1a}}

===Sabbat Worlds Crusade===
Vadim's head for heights came in handy for the regiment's deployment on [[Phantine (Planet)|Phantine]]; due to the fact that Phantine's cities were perched atop mountain peaks above [[The Scald|a layer of pollution]], many of the Militarum operations on the planet involved aerial combat drops.{{Fn|1a}}

During the assault on the city of [[Cirenholm]], the [[drop-ship]] Vadim's squad was on was shot down and crash landed on the exterior of the city's secondary dome.{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}} As the survivors of the crash regrouped, Vadim was responsible for rescuing a number of Guardsmen who had slid off the roof in the chaos and had been caught by their ropes snagging on protrusions just over the edge of the dome.{{Fn|1c}}

Following the taking of Cirenholm, Vadim was selected personally by [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]] as one of sixteen Tanith Guardsmen assigned to [[Operation Larisel]], the mission to infiltrate the city of [[Ouranberg]] and assassinate [[Sagittar Slaith]], the commander of the [[Blood Pact]] forces active on Phantine.{{Fn|1d}}

