Nuadhu 'Fireheart'.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Wild Rider]] of [[Saim Hann]]'s [[Clan Fireheart]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
[[Image:Nuadhu.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|4e}}]]
Nuadhu is a legendary [[Vyper]] rider that rides standing up to aid in his attacks. He is the heir of [[Clan Fireheart]], which is led by his ailing father [[Naiall Fireheart]] and half-sister [[Caelledhin]].{{Fn|4a}} He is also considered reckless, paying no heed to danger and gladly flying straight into the heaviest enemy fire. His Wild Riders also follow him into the fiercest fighting.{{Fn|1}}

In mid-[[M39]], he led his Craftworld's forces in slaying the [[Daemon Prince]] of [[Slaanesh]] [[Lilesh Snarelust]], plunging his own [[Celestial Lance]] into the Daemon's Heart.{{Fn|2}} He also took part in the [[Pyrus Reach Conflict]].{{Fn|3}}

At the end of the [[41st Millennium]], Nuadhu, Naiall, and Caelledhin all journey to the ''[[Ynnead's Dream]]'' to request aid from the [[Ynnari]] in battling [[Necrons]] on [[Agarimethea]].{{Fn|4a}} Believing that the final [[Cronesword]] may lie on the world, Yvraine agreed and her forces take part in the raid alongside other Saim-Hann forces.{{Fn|4b}} During the battle against [[Necron]]s and later inadvertently released [[Daemon]]s, it was revealed by Yvraine that Naiall had been unintentionally harboring the soul of his first wife and Caelledhin's mother, [[Iyothia Icewhisper]], within him which explained his decline in health. Nuadhu and Caelledhin are able to get Naiall to relinquish her soul, allowing Yvraine to use her power to break through the Necron null-field and reconnect with [[Ynnead]] briefly and turn the tide of the battle.{{Fn|4d}} In the final stage of the battle, Caelledhin sacrificed herself to seal the [[Warp]] portal at the center of the Necron tomb complex. Nuadhu, grieving his half-sister but changed by the experience, departed back to Saim-Hann and contemplated on his place in his Clans future now that his father is back to full health.{{Fn|4d}}

==Alean – The Steed of Khaine==
Nuadhu rides upon a  Vyper that has been built to allow  him to fight on its  back, much as [[Khaine]] rode to war on the legendary steed [[Alean]].{{Fn|1}}

