{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
{{ambig|subject=[[Sanguinary Priest]]|disambiguation=Numitor}}
'''Numitor''' was a [[Sanguinary High Priest]] of the [[Blood Angels]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
He was among the Blood Angels the Chapter committed to the fight against [[Ezekyle Abaddon|the Despoiler's]] hordes in the [[13th Black Crusade]]; Numitor's force added their strength to the [[Battle of the Agripinaa System|defence]] of [[Agripinaa]] from [[Kossolax|Kossolax the Foresworn]], an infamous [[Champion of Khorne]].{{Fn|1}}

At one point in the fighting, Kossolax sacrificed a number of his [[World Eaters]] to summon forth a mighty [[Bloodthirster]]. Numitor confronted the [[daemon]] and managed to stun the creature, only for it to sever Numitor's arm with a crack of [[Lash of Khorne|its whip]]. This caused Numitor to drop the [[Blood Chalice|grail]] he was holding, spilling the blood of [[Sanguinius]] contained within it.{{Fn|1}}

The sight of their [[Primarch|Primarch's]] spilled blood, combined with Numitor yelling the words of the [[Rite of Exsanguination]], caused the assembled [[Death Company|Death Company Marines]] to go berserk and charge the Bloodthirster, cutting it down at the cost of half their number before unleashing their unstoppable rage against Kossolax's warriors. Although the [[Imperial]]s were able to drive the World Eaters off of Agripinaa, Kossolax escaped and Numitor has vowed to hunt him down.{{Fn|1}}

