Nyxos.wikitext:
{{OrdoMalleusPortal}}
An [[Inquisitor Lord]] of the [[Ordo Malleus]] during the time of the [[13th Black Crusade]], '''Nyxos''' worked closely with the [[Grey Knights]], especially [[Justicar]] [[Alaric]].

==Biography==
It is reported he has been in service to the [[Emperor of Mankind|Emperor's]] [[Inquisition]] for several centuries.{{Fn|1}} He appears as a tired, frail old man, given to wise-cracking. His frame is supported by a servo-assisted exoskeleton, which in fact makes him much stronger and more resilient than humans a fraction of his age.{{Fn|1}}

===Valinov===
During the [[13th Black Crusade]] in 999.[[M41]], Nyxos oversaw the [[Ordo Malleus]]'s response to the threat of the Prince of a Thousand Faces, [[Ghargatuloth]] and his impending resurrection into realspace. While meeting with the [[Grey Knights Grand Master|Grand Master]]s on [[Titan (Moon)|Titan]], Nyxos suggested that [[Alaric]] should lead the assault force against the [[Daemon Prince]]. He assigned Inquisitor [[Ligeia]] to lead the investigative part of the mission, using her unique [[psychic]] abilities to draw information out of records.{{Fn|1}}

As Nyxos was observing the execution of [[Radical]] Inquisitor [[Valinov]] at the [[Encaladus]] prison complex on [[Saturn]], Ligeia's personal [[Death Cult Assassin]]s appeared and aided Valinov's escape. Nyxos would have been mortally wounded in his duel with the culists and Valinov, had it not been for the many redundant organs that kept him alive.{{Fn|1}} Ultimately, he was forced to condemn Ligeia to death, as she had become corrupted after opening her mind to Ghargatuloth, even though doing so had allowed her to find a way to defeat him.{{Fn|1}}

After the daemon was banished to the [[warp]], Nyxos went to the Ordo Malleus's archive and supervised the careful inscription of the daemon's [[True Name]] into the [[Codicium Aeternum]].{{Fn|1}}

===Dark Adeptus===
After the events on [[Volcanis Ultor]], Nyxos took his retinue to investigate the appearance of a planet that appeared from the warp that had been missing for one hundred years. As it turned out the planet was a missing [[forge world]], [[Chaeronia]], and Nyxos was forced to politically grapple with the [[Mechanicus]] to get a force down and investigate the events on the planet while he stayed with the small fleet in orbit.{{Fn|2}}

The fleet was attacked by a [[Chaos]] fleet led by [[Urkrathos]], [[Chosen of Abaddon]]. Once again it was the assistance of his many augmentations that kept him alive while the ship he was on depressurized.{{Fn|2}} As before, he was primarily responsible for debriefing Alaric and compiling his findings into a report for the leadership of the [[Inquisition]].{{Fn|2}}

===Lost Friends===
After believing that Alaric was lost on Sarthis Marjoris he later received a communication from him on the ex-[[Pleasure world]] [[Belsimar]] and recovered him back into the Imperial fold. Nyxos made light to Alaric that he could assist him in going back to the Grey Knights, but he also hinted that a [[Space Marine]] with imagination like his could serve the Inquisition so much more as something else and left it at that.{{Fn|3}}

==Retinue==
As an Inquisitor, Nyxos has the power to commandeer anyone or anything to complete his holy duty to the [[Golden Throne]]. Throughout his known history he has requested the assistance of the Grey Knights, the [[Cruiser]] ''Tribunicia'', the explorator Mechanicus ship ''Exemplar'' and regiments of [[Imperial Guard]]. His only permanent known retinue would be an ex-naval cadet [[Hawkespur]] who is a young starched uniform woman who is a crack shot with her pistol. She is currently enlisted to Nyxos as his [[interrogator]].{{Cite This}}

