Omin Lund.wikitext:
{{WIP}}
{{spoiler|source=Missing in Action (Short Story)}}
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Omin Lund''' was a [[Guardsman]] of the [[Ninth Sameter Infantry]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|Regiment]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
Following the [[Surealis Campaign]], Lund and a number of other Guardsmen from the Ninth Sameter were allowed to return to Sameter and retire. Lund became a bartender in the city of [[Urbitane]]. However, after the horrors they witnessed in the [[Battle of Klodeshi Heights]], many of the veterans developed severe shellshock. Believing that [[heretic]]s had infiltrated Urbitane all around them, the former Guardsmen started ritually murdering a number of the "heretics".{{Fn|1}}

One of their victims was [[Luthar Hewall]], a rug-maker, whose body was discovered in a soil-stack near Lund's bar. His death was linked to the similar deaths of [[Idilane Fasple]] and [[Poul Grevan]]. As a result, the city's [[Arbites]] garrison believed that a [[Chaos Cult]] was active in Urbitane; they requested the aid of [[Inquisitor]] [[Gregor Eisenhorn]] (who was present in Urbitane investigating an unrelated matter).{{Fn|1}}

When Eisenhorn and his [[Inquisitorial Retinue|retinue]] were investigating around the area where Hewall's body was discovered, he met Lund and interrogated her, but learned little. However, he noticed Lund's [[tattoo]] (the symbol of the Sameter Ninth).{{Fn|1}}

Later, after Eisenhorn had pieced together the identities of the killers and rounded up most of the surviving Guardsmen, he tracked the remainder down to the Sameter Agricultural Fraternity Guildhall. There, he tried to convince them that their war was over and that they could stand down, but a firefight ensued. All of the Guardsmen in the guildhall were killed.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
