Orac Myriad.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Orac Myriad''' was a hyper-advanced [[Abominable Intelligence]], that steered the [[Daemon|Demi-Chaos God]] [[Vashtorr]]'s  [[Ark of Omen]], ''[[Orac Unleashed]]''.{{Fn|1}}

==History==
Through circumstances unknown, the Orac Myriad first appeared in a [[Cogitator]] device used by [[Ordo Astartes]] [[Inquisitor]] [[Hallex]] to locate [[The Rock]]. The Inquisitor was unaware of the entity's presence within his own Cogitator as he spied on the Dark Angels.{{Fn|2}}

During the [[Arks of Omen Campaign]], Vashtorr sought to capture a [[Key-Fragment]] from the [[Dark Angels]]' [[Fortress Monastery]] and tasked the Myriad's infinite algorithmic cunning to locate it and plan the perfect ambush. This led to Vashtorr using his powerful abilities to make the ''Orac Unleashed'' and the fleets of his [[Black Legion]] and [[Word Bearers]] allies appear out of the [[Warp]] just as the [[Chapter]] was coming to the aid of the beleaguered [[Imperial]] world [[Marwent's Reach]].{{Fn|1}}  

Later during the [[Battle of Idolatros]], Vashtorr utilized the ''Orac Unleashed'' and its AI against The Rock. However after assembling the last components of the [[Dissonance Engine]], the Ark of Omen was abandoned by Vashtorr as the Orac Myriad howled in betrayal and despair. The Ark was subsequently destroyed by the Imperial fleet.{{Fn|3}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*Orac was a supercomputer in the British science fiction series ''[[wikipedia:Blake's 7|Blake's 7]]'' who acted as the advisor to the protagonists of the show.

