Oris.wikitext:
{{AdeptaSororitasPortal}}
'''Oris''' is an [[Order of Our Martyred Lady]] [[Canoness Preceptor]], who is a veteran of countless battles.{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:Oris.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Oris{{Fn|1}}]]
In [[M42]], she was part of an [[Imperial]] fleet, that was sent to end a [[Chaos]] rebellion on the vital [[Mining World]] [[Siscia]]. Oris had command of the [[Retribution Class Battleship]] [[Fiery Heart (Battleship)|Fiery Heart]], which was sent by the fleet to Siscia as its vanguard. Her forces would then invade the world, when the rest of the fleet arrived there. However as her forces prepared themselves, Oris was approached by the [[Ordo Hereticus]] [[Inquisitor]] [[Ander]], who sought her assistance. Before the rebellion had begun, Ander had sent one of his [[Acolyte]]s to Siscia, in search of a powerful object and to discover who led the Cult. This was before it became such a dire threat and Ander had lost contact with his Acolyte since the uprising began.{{Fn|1}} 

The [[Inquisitor]] asked that Oris, secretly send an efficient force of [[Adepta Sororitas]] to recover the lost [[Acolyte]], before the fleet's invasion began. He also asked that a [[Sister Dialogus]] accompany the force and that Oris use her resources to decipher encrypted letters, the Acolyte had sent him. Oris would do so and sent a force of 8 [[Adepta Sororitas|Sororitas]] to [[Siscia]], who were led by [[Canoness]] [[Veridyan]]. When he learned of this, [[Ander]] questioned why Oris would send such a small force, given the importance of their mission. She replied that given the [[Inquisitor]]'s requirements, the Sororitas she had sent would be enough to successfully find the Acolyte. However, the little information they had gathered from Siscia described a deteriorating situation, filled with too many contradictions. Too many things about the rebellion were also not adding up and the fleet's invasion would happen soon. This left her feeling out of her depth and Oris now harbored hidden doubts about Veridyan's chance of succeeding in her mission.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
