Orm Hendriksen.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}{{DeathwatchPortal}}
'''Orm Hendriksen''' is a [[Space Wolves]] [[Rune Priest]]{{Fn|1a}}, who served in the [[Wolf Lord]] [[Ragnar Blackmane]]'s [[Blackmanes|Great Company]]{{Fn|1b}} before joining the [[Death Watch]]. However for the last 96 years, he has served in the retinue of the [[Radical]] [[Lord Inquisitor]] [[Tytonida Nebaszinar Falx|Falx]], whose dubious standing with the [[Ordo Xenos]] matches Hendriksen's within the [[Deathwatch]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
The two met in late [[M41]], when Hendriksen's [[Kill-Team]] encountered a drunk [[Tytonida Nebaszinar Falx|Falx]] in a bar, while conducting a mission. The belligerent [[Lord Inquisitor]] swung at the Kill-Team's [[Watch Sergeant|Sergeant]], an action which would have led to her death had Hendriksen not intervened. Though he suspected Falx had done so because she wished to die, the Lord Inquisitor's continued boldness and audacity in face of certain death earned his respect. This led him to join Falx's retinue aboard the [[Severissimus Exactor‎]], where he tried to prevent Falx from taking the type of [[Radical]] actions, that led to her low standing within the [[Ordo Xenos]]. However Hendriksen knows that once the Lord Inquisitor's mind is made up, there is little he can do but stand by her side and defend Falx from the fallout of her reckless decisions.{{Fn|1c}} 

In [[M42]], [[Tytonida Nebaszinar Falx|Falx]] added the [[Ogryn]] [[Cassia (Ogryn)|Cassia]] to her retinue, after it was discovered the [[Abhuman]] was a [[Psyker]]. Though this went against what was established by the [[Imperial Truth]], Cassia's psychic powers were real and Hendriksen took on the role as a mentor to her. He was dedicated to ensuring Cassia made the best of her abilities and that the Ogryn did not fall to [[Heresy]] because of them. Though the two constantly sniped at each other, the Lord Inquisitor knew that any real enmity between them, was now buried under mutually developed respect{{Fn|1a}}. However while Hendriksen loyally serves Falx, his pride has prevented him from telling the Inquisitor that he is dangerously close to falling to the [[Space Wolves]]' [[Wulfen]] curse.{{Fn|1b}}

Falx ultimately was able to capture [[Makari]], the [[Ork]] [[Gretchin]] who was the banner waver of the infamous [[Warboss]] [[Ghazghkull Mag Uruk Thraka]]. Falx and her retinue then used the Ork [[Biter (Blood Axe)|Biter]] as an interpreter.{{Fn|1a}} After hearing Makari's tale, the Inquisition group is betrayed by Biter, who uses his security clearance to alert an incoming Ork fleet. The fate of the Imperials is left ambiguous but it is implied they were unable to escape.{{Fn|1d}}

