Orthos Ulatal.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Orthos Ulatal''' was a [[Rage Fighter|starfighter]] pilot and [[Legiones Auxilia|auxiliary]] attached to the [[Night Lords]] [[Space Marine Legion]] during the [[Great Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
By one point in the Crusade, Ulatal was [[Wing Commander|Commander]] of a [[Imperial Fighter Wings|fighter wing]], assigned to the VIII Legion's [[Legiones Auxilia|Auxiliary corps]]. Although not a native of [[Nostramo]], during his time with the Legion he became fluent in several Nostraman dialects. His career ended in a crash during an engagement on [[Juuvaur]], in which Ulatal suffered severe and lasting injuries. He survived the incident but was left dependant on life support, unable to continue flying and so was removed from active duty. His wingmate and second-in-command, [[Perdita (Wing Commander)|Perdita]], was promoted to replace him.{{Fn|1}}

Following this, Ulatal was seconded to [[Crusade Battlefleet Archival Services]], still attached to the VIII Legion. He spent much of his time stationed on board the VIII Legion vessel ''[[Serpent of the Black Seas]]'', filing reports on the Legion's campaigns (although many thought that, due to the heroism attached to the events on Juuvaur, the Crusade staff might eventually promote him to command of a larger [[Imperialis Armada|Armada]] vessel or a [[Wing Captain|fighter group captain]] on a carrier vessel). This continued until Ulatal came across a personal log on a [[data-slate]] written by [[Iskandar Khayon|Khayon]], a [[Legionary]] of the [[Thousand Sons]], concerning [[Devastation of Zoah|a joint operation]] between his Legion and the Night Lords on the planet [[Zoah]]. The report on the slate alleged that the two Legions' [[primarch]]s, [[Konrad Curze]] and [[Magnus the Red]], nearly came to blows in the aftermath of the campaign following a disagreement over the fate of [[Tower of Serenity|a repository]] of [[warp]] lore on the planet. A number of details in the report caught Ulatal's attention, however: in particular the fact that Khayon had filed his report unofficially and behind his superiors' backs and that it cast the Night Lords in an extremely negative light. This left him unsure as to whether to file the report or not.{{Fn|1}}

Due to the nature of the report and Ulatal's own curiosity, he spent weeks travelling on cargo vessels until he eventually rendezvoused with the Night Lords' flagship, the ''[[Nightfall]]'', in order to speak to one of the Legion's archivists. After waiting for three days, he finally received a response but not from a mere [[Legion serf|serf]] - he was paid a visit by none other than [[Jago Sevatarion|Sevatar]], the Legion's [[First Captain]]. Sevatar proceeded to give Ulatal an ultimatum: he could file the report as it was, or delete it, and return to his posting, or Sevatar could show him the truth. Ulatal, despite suspecting that Sevatar would kill him for learning his secrets, watched the Captain's personal log on the Zoah campaign and the clash between the two primarchs.{{Fn|1}}

After the recording was over, Sevatar stood before Ulatal, preparing to execute him due to Crusade mandates about supressing knowledge of disunity between the primarchs. Before he struck, however, the ''Nightfall's'' commander, [[Shang]], voxed a message to Sevatar, telling him that Ulatal had received his promotion and had been assigned as a group captain aboard the ''[[Voidmaw]]''. His ultimate fate is unknown.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The Abyssal Edge (Short Story)]] — [[Sons of the Emperor (Anthology)]]

