Osmadiel.wikitext:
{{DarkAngelsPortal}}
[[Image:Osmadiel.jpg|thumb|right|Osmadiel{{Fn|1}}]]
{{Spoiler|source=Battlefleet Gothic: Armada II}}
'''Osmadiel''' is a [[Fallen Angel]] [[Space Marine Captain|Master]], who is reformed and once again loyal to the [[Imperium]]. Fighting in the Emperor's name while in a self-imposed exile, he waits for the day the Dark Angels can leave the past behind. He has command of a sizable force of Fallen Angels, who share his values.{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
In the aftermath of [[Cadia]]'s [[13th Black Crusade|destruction]], [[Segmentum Obscurus]] became a massive war zone and a [[Chaos]] fleet threatened to claim [[Caliban]]'s remains. This led Osmadiel and his fleet to return from their self-imposed seclusion, in order to defend their destroyed [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]]. However the Chaos fleet's numbers would be too much for Osmadiel and during the battle, he sent out a plea for any Imperial forces nearby to aid his fleet. The [[Imperial Navy]] [[Lord High Admiral]] [[Spire]] would answer and his fleet aided Osmadiel in destroying the Chaos fleet, earning the Fallen Angels thanks.{{Fn|1}}  

Soon afterwards, though, the fleet of the [[Dark Angels]] [[Space Marine Captain|Master]] [[Korahael]] appeared and confronted both of them. [[Spire]] was surprised to see Korahael, as he thought the Dark Angel had been{{Fn|1}} slain in [[Cadia]]'s [[13th Black Crusade|death throes]]{{Fn|2}}. Korahael remarked in reply that his supposed death, was a common misconception. He then declared that by order of [[Dark Angels Supreme Grand Master|Supreme Grand Master]] [[Azrael]], Spire would join his fleet and attack Osmadiel, who was a traitor to the [[Imperium]]. If the Admiral did so, the Dark Angels would forgive him for aiding Osmadiel. The Fallen Angel replied he should have known that the [[Destruction of Caliban|wounds]] between the Fallen and the Dark Angels have not healed, despite the millennia that has passed. Korahael told Osmadiel that there was no redemption for the Fallen, only the absolution of death. Spire meanwhile, was unaware of the conflict between the two groups and stated he did not understand what was going on. Osmadiel declared that no explanation would serve the Admiral and that he had no part in the battle between the two Masters. He then asked if that Spire had any respect for the victory they just achieved, then the Admiral should stand down and not interfere. Korahael, though, claimed that Spire's duty to the Imperium required the Admiral to fight the traitorous Osmadiel. It is not known however, what the final outcome of the battle was.{{Fn|1}}

==Notes==
The outcome of the battle depends on the decision, the player controlling [[Spire]] makes. If the player joins Osmadiel, then the player's forces withdraw without engaging Korahael, whose fate is left unknown. Korahael will tell Spire he has chosen poorly, while Osmadiel will respond that Spire shows greater wisdom than either of them. Osmadiel will return to seclusion to continue the fight against Chaos from exile. If the player joins Korahael, then Osmadiel and his [[Fallen Angels]] will die. Afterwards, the Master that was chosen will aid Spire; Korahael providing his forces to the [[Lord High Admiral]] as he seeks to restore the [[Imperium]]'s rule to the embattled [[Segmentum Obscurus]], and Osmadiel reappearing to assist Spire in the final battle against [[Abaddon the Despoiler]].{{Fn|1}}

