Oud Oudia Raskian.wikitext:
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
'''Oud Oudia Raskian''' was the [[Fabricator-General]] of [[Mars]] and served as one of the [[High Lord of Terra]], during the [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}} Raskian also led the [[Martian Synod]].{{Fn|4a}}

== Biography ==
Due to his extensive cybernetic augmentation, Oud was more building than man and thus was the most difficult High Lord to speak to directly. Moving his form to the [[Great Chamber of the Senatorum Imperialis]] required extensive logistical work and construction. During the Fall of [[Cadia]], he was among the High Lords most against the proposal of dissolving the [[Edict of Restraint]] put forth by [[Chancellor of the Imperial Council]] [[Lev Tieron]] that would have allowed the [[Adeptus Custodes]] to leave Terra.{{Fn|1b}} Accoring to Tieron, what Raskian fears most is that his organizations uncertainty over the very technology they claim mastery over is exposed.{{Fn|1c}}

Alongside [[Master of the Astronomican]] [[Leops Franck]] and [[Speaker for the Chartist Captains]] [[Kania Dhanda]] {{PAGENAME}} was one of the three High Lords of Terra who collaborated with [[Lord Inquisitor]] [[Adamara Rassilo]] to smuggle a [[Dark Eldar]] [[Haemonculus]] onto [[Terra]] in order to repair the failing [[Golden Throne]].{{Fn|2}}

Raskian eventually traveled into [[Commorragh]] itself to complete his transactions with [[Archon]] [[Shae-Morvain]] of the [[Kabal of the Still-Living Knife]], though according to [[Erasmus Crowl]] his plan only delayed the death of the [[Golden Throne]] by a few centuries. Crowl, his retinue, and the [[Custodian]] [[Navradaran]] intervened and caused fighting to break out between the [[Imperium]] and the Kabal's forces. As the two sides tore at each other, Raskian's core unit attempted to flee.{{Fn|3}}

Afterwards Raskian was declared missing and presumed dead. A New Fabricator-General was appointed in his place.{{Fn|5}}

=== Cawl & Raskian ===
Rumors spread that [[Magos Dominus|Archmagos Dominus]] [[Belisarius Cawl|Cawl]] sought to use his powerful position within the [[Imperium]] to replace Raskian as [[Mars]]' [[Fabricator-General]]. However when he was directly asked about this, during a [[Conclave Chronalis|conclave]] with several high-ranking [[Magos|Magi]] of the [[Adeptus Mechanicus]], Cawl denied he had any desire to do so, and that even if he truly wanted to he did not have the means to replace Raskian.{{Fn|4c}} However, Raskian still hates Cawl. The Archmagos believes that the Fabricator General fears he has gone rogue and seeks to gather enough followers and power in order to supplant him as Fabricator General of Mars.{{Fn|4b}}

