Parchett.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Parchett''' is a [[Scribe]] in the [[Imperium]]'s [[Administratum]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
[[Image:Parchett.jpg|thumb|right|220px|[[Scribe]] Parchett{{Fn|1b}}]]
He was assigned to the [[Mordian 24th]] [[Regiment]], during the [[Third War for Armageddon]] and was tasked with recording the outcome of the conflict for the [[Administratum]]'s records.{{Fn|1b}} When the 24th was set to counter-attack against [[Ork]] forces on the '''Sulphur River''', however,{{Fn|1a}} Parchett was left behind, along with the other civilians attached to the Regiment. Instead, they were placed with [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] [[Kaine (Captain)|Kaine]]'s [[Platoon|3rd Platoon]],{{Fn|1b}} which was charged with guarding the 24th's supplies, within a ruined mine close to the Sulphur River's '''Asch Creek''', until the Regiment returned. Unfortunately disaster struck soon afterwards, when the 24th was almost completely destroyed by an Ork ambush and its few survivors were unable to warn Kaine about their defeat. An Ork [[Warboss]] then led a horde against the unsuspecting Platoon{{Fn|1a}}, along with Parchett, the [[Ratling Sniper]] [[Hookey (Mordian Iron Guard)|Hookey]], the 24th's Hive Militia and other civilians the Regiment left behind as well.{{Fn|1b}} Though vastly outnumbered, the 3rd is unaware that the Orks only have a limited time to battle the Platoon, before the horde has to return to the Xenos' main camp.{{Fn|1a}} Should he survive the Orks' attack, Parchett will write about the 3rd Platoon's victory, which will mark it among the famous ones won by the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|1b}} 
==Trivia==
*The [[Mordian 24th]]{{Fn|1a}} and [[Parchett]]{{Fn|1b}} were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Jervis Johnson]]. They were featured in [[Citadel Journal 48]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}
*The ''Last Stand at Asch Creek'' is a modified version of the [[Battle of Glazer's River]] scenario, which appeared in [[White Dwarf 222 (UK)]]. Besides the change in [[Regiment]] and location,{{Fn|1a}} the [[Platoon]] is led by [[Kaine (Captain)|Kaine]], instead of [[Caine (Captain)|Caine]]. The names of the characters Hookey and Blikk, however, remain the same.{{Fn|1b}} 

