Phael Toron.wikitext:
{{ThousandSonsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Captain]] of the [[Thousand Sons]] during the [[Great Crusade]]{{Fn|1a}} and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1d}}

==Biography==
A member of the [[Cults_of_the_Thousand_Sons#Cult_of_the_Raptora|Raptora Cult]], he commanded the 7th [[Fellowship]], which spent most of the Crusade on [[Prospero]] as part of its defense force and as a training cadre for potential [[Aspirant]]s.{{fn|1a}}{{fn|1b}} As such, he and his subordinates had to adapt to the newfound arcana the rest of the Legion brought back from their travels, and he was ill at ease with the paraphernalia involved in more advanced rituals.{{fn|1b}}{{fn|1c}}

During the [[Burning of Prospero]], Phael Toron and his Fellowship were deployed in the outer precincts of [[Tizca]]'s naval port. A proponent of using psychic abilities only as a last resort, he controlled his [[Tutelary]] Dtoaa's desire to unleash their combined power upon the invaders, believing his Fellowship to be as of yet too unaccustomed to the new knowledge. To the behest of his [[Philosophus]] [[Tulekh]], he authorized the use of psykana, embracing his impressive [[Psychic]] abilities and causing heavy casualties against the [[Space Wolves]] as the first signs of the flesh change manifested themselves. However he lost control, Dtoaa feeding him far more [[Warp]] energy than he could master, and his body to overloaded into a kilometer-wide explosion.{{Fn|1d}}

