'''Phra-Mu Coparnos''' was an [[Arcanalyst]] [[Tech-Priest]], who served in the [[Indomitus Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
He was among the [[Imperial]] forces assigned to a [[Torchbearer Fleet]] that is searching for the [[Knights of Mhorwen]] [[Chapter]]. However, the fleet had trouble finding the Chapter and travelled to a ruined [[Forge World]] which they believed had dealings with the Knights. To find the information, a small force consisting of [[Skitarii]], led by Coparnos, [[Adeptus Custodes|Custodes]] [[Emissaries Imperatus|Emissaries]], led by [[Regh Thalian Demetriad|Demetriad]] and [[Sisters of Silence]], led by [[Vhorlia]], were sent to the world. Coparnos discovered the information was located within the data-core of the '''Archivolt Quranos''' [[Forge Temple]] and later found its location. Upon entering the Forge Temple, however, the Torchbearers were attacked by hordes of corrupted [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] constructs.{{Fn|1}} 

It was then revealed that the ruined [[Forge World]] had been invaded and then infected by [[Scrap Code]]s, which caused the '''Archivolt''' to create the mechanical hordes. The [[Torchbearers]] were heavily outnumbered and they suffered heavy losses before Coparnos reached the data-core. Though he risked corrupting himself, the [[Tech-Priest]] connected with it and was able to find the [[Knights of Mhorwen|Knights]]' location. However, he was unable to disconnect quickly enough and became infected by the Scrap Code. As Coparnos' body became [[Chaos|corrupted]], the Tech-Priest gave the information to Demetriad and pleaded with him to escape and find the Knights. While the mechanical hordes continued to attack the Torchbearers, Demetriad gathered the handful that were left and began leading them out of the Archivot. Coparnos then begged the [[Omnissiah]] to light the Torchbearers' path to the Knights, before the Tech-Priest's consciousness left him.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[White Dwarf 466]], pgs. 56-59 - ''[[The Hunt for Mhorwen (Short Story)]]''

{{DEFAULTSORT:Coparnos, Phra-Mu}}

