Qope Halver.wikitext:
{{AlphaLegionPortal}}
'''Qope Halver''' is a [[Headhunter|Headhunter Prime]] in the [[Serpent's Teeth]] [[Alpha Legion]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]].
==History==
In [[M42]], he took part in the [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]'s invasion of the [[Imperial]] world [[Pendata (World)|Pendata]] for its resources. The [[Silver Templars]]' [[Indomitus Crusade]] forces would later come to the world's aid, however, and caused the [[Serpent's Teeth]] to leave the world empty handed.{{Fn|1}}

He is present when [[Harrowmaster]] [[Solomon Akurra]] calls for a meeting of Alpha Legion warbands on the ''Unseen'', and the two quietly discuss the myriad of warriors the Legion has become.{{Fn|1}}

When Akurra was seemingly killed by [[Lord Discordant]] [[Xettus Qeele]] in a secret usurpation, he grudgingly admitted despite their differences that Akurra was a much preferred Harrowmaster to the arrogance of Qeele. He and his Headhunters later encounter a battle-scarred Akurra and his [[Rogue Psyker]] [[Tulava Dyne]] in the vents of an Adeptus Mechanics facility who save them from a combat servitor ambush. Akurra asks him if he intends to slay him and bring Qeele his corpse to gain favour, citing Halver's dislike of him. Halver shrewdly replies that such an action would alert the Lord Discordant that Halver was aware of his betrayal, and he could simply flip the board on Halver and claim to the rest of the warband that he was the traitor instead. He agrees to assist Akurra secretly rejoin the warband.{{Fn|1}}

When Qeele leads a victory parade down onto [[Qampar]] to declare the Alpha Legion's victory over the Imperial defenders, Halver and his [[Headhunter|Headhunters]] prowl the rooftops as security. When the Silver Templars spring a final ambush on the parade, they move to protect Qeele but run into eleven [[Primaris Space Marine|Primaris]] Silver Templars emerging from underground, who are also taken by surprise. The Headhunters emerge victorious but Halver is shot in the gut in the fighting. His fate is unknown.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
