Quater Traves.wikitext:
{{WIP}}
{{spoiler|source=Missing in Action (Short Story)}}
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Quater Traves''' was a [[Guardsman]] of the [[Ninth Sameter Infantry]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|Regiment]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
Following the campaign on [[Surealis]], Traves and a number of other Guardsmen from the Ninth Sameter were allowed to return to Sameter and retire. Traves became the supervisor for a tenement [[hab]] in the city of [[Urbitane]]. However, after the horrors they witnessed in the [[Battle of Klodeshi Heights]], many of the veterans developed severe shellshock. Believing that [[heretic]]s had infiltrated Urbitane all around them, the former Guardsmen started ritually murdering a number of the "heretics".{{Fn|1}}

One of their victims was [[Idilane Fasple]], a midwife. When Fasple's body was discovered in the crawlspace within Traves's tenement's roof, her death was linked to the similar deaths of [[Luthar Hewall]] and [[Poul Grevan]]. As a result, the city's [[Arbites]] garrison believed that a [[Chaos Cult]] was active in Urbitane; they requested the aid of [[Inquisitor]] [[Gregor Eisenhorn]] (who was present in Urbitane investigating an unrelated matter).{{Fn|1}}

When Eisenhorn and his [[Inquisitorial Retinue|retinue]] were investigating the tenement where Fasple's body was found, he met Traves and interrogated him, but learned little. However, he noticed Traves's signet ring (marked with the symbol of the Sameter Ninth).{{Fn|1}}

Later, after Eisenhorn had pieced together the identities of the killers and rounded up most of the surviving Guardsmen, he tracked the remainder down to the Sameter Agricultural Fraternity Guildhall. There, he tried to convince them that their war was over and that they could stand down, but a firefight ensued. All of the Guardsmen in the guildhall were killed.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Missing in Action (Short Story)]]

