Queue.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinePortal}}
'''Queue''' was a former [[Master of the Forge|Chief Armourer]] of the [[Darting Blades]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
In [[M37]], he was known for his legendary genius and esoteric creations, which Queue tested in the [[Chapter]]'s famous '''Armourer's Chapel''' [[Armoury]].{{Fn|1b}} This included the [[Harpoon Gun (Terminator)|Harpoon Gun]], the [[GSRC Bolter]], the [[Mk13 Battering Ram]], the [[Quadruple Bolter]]{{Fn|1a}} and several booby traps. However, despite his genius, Queue had the flaw of being absentminded. This led to disastrous results in the fiftieth year of M37, as Queue was testing his latest booby trap, which he had disguised as a [[S15 Field Tool Box]]. This was done through the use of a [[Automated Test Dummy]], whose behaviour was a facsimile of an [[Ork]] [[Gretchin]].{{Fn|1b}} 

However when the Dummy's given Gretchin behaviour led it to open the Tool Box, nothing happened. Watching from a nearby bunker alongside several of his fellow [[Darting Blades]], including the [[Techmarine|Armourer]] [[Mathias (Darting Blades)|Mathias]], an angry Queue gathered his tools to find out what had gone wrong. When the [[Master of the Forge|Chief Armourer]] could not find the correct type of [[screwdriver]] he needed, Queue opened a Field Box he had placed within the bunker. As Queue began to lift its lid, however, Mathias realised that the Chief Armourer had mistakenly mixed up the placements of the Field Boxes. Before the Armourer could warn Queue, though, the booby trapped Field Box exploded within the bunker and killed the Chief Armourer. Several Darting Blades were killed as well, by the explosion and Mathias and others were left severely wounded.{{Fn|1b}}

Queue's creations outlived their creator and are still used by [[Space Marines]]. However they are now considered to be obsolete, due to the [[Imperium]] having access to more efficient and modern designs.{{Fn|1a}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*''Queue'' and the [[Darting Blades]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Richard Halliwell]]. They appeared in [[The Citadel Journal 7]].{{Fn|1b}}
*The character is a reference to [[Wikipedia:Q (James Bond)|Q]], a character from the ''[[Wikipedia:James Bond|James Bond]]'' franchise who provides the titular secret agent with his weapons and gadgets.

==Sources==
