Rakhim.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
{{Fanatic}}
'''Rakhim''' was a [[Force Commander]], in the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]] and was considered an honorable hero.{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He had command of the [[Pride of Fenris]], when it received a [[Operation Salvation|plea for aid]] from [[Asedor]]. Rakhim then led his forces to the [[Imperial]] [[Hive World]], but discovered that it was firmly in control of the [[Brothers of Retaliation]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] and their [[Chaos Cult]] and [[Traitor Guard|Traitor PDF]] allies. Seeing this, led the [[Force Commander]] to know that his forces were outnumbered and could not win in a direct assault against the invaders. Instead he sought to escort Asedor's [[Imperial Governor]], [[Elias An'Therosed]], to the Pride of Fenris, so the Governor could provide intelligence about the [[Chaos]] forces they would face. This would then allow the [[Space Wolves]] to know where to aim their attacks, in order to ensure they defeated the invaders. Verodan was then part of the rescue-team that Rakhim led to extract An-Therosed and it [[teleported]] to the Governor's besieged palace in the '''Arden Prime''' [[Hive]].{{Fn|1}} 

They found [[Elias An'Therosed|An'Therosed]] with his remaining loyal forces and were preparing to [[teleport]] back to the [[Pride of Fenris]], when disaster struck. The [[Brothers of Retaliation]] became aware of the [[Space Wolves]]' presence and jammed the rescue-team's teleport signal. This prevented them from escaping with An'Therosed and with [[Asedor]]'s orbital defenses in the [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]'s hands, the Pride of Fenris was also unable to send [[Thunderhawks]] to extract the Space Wolves and Governor. The Chaos invaders then attacked them, but An'Therosed informed the rescue-team that there was a prototype [[Escape Pod]], at the top of '''Arden Prime''''s [[Hive-spire]]. While it could not house all of them, the Escape Pod was made to be invisible to sensors and could safely reach the Pride of Fenris. But they would need to reach it before the Chaos invaders broke through their defensive lines. Acting quickly, the Space Wolves began escorting the Governor to the Escape Pod chamber, while leaving An'Therosed's remaining loyal Adeptus Arbites and Guardsmen to fended off the invaders. However the [[Chaos]] forces overran the Governor's forces and a group of the Brothers of Retaliation began pursing the rescue-team. The [[Chaos Space Marines]] were then able to catch up with the Space Wolves, as they neared the Escape Pod's chamber.{{Fn|1}} 

In the intense fighting that erupted, both sides suffered numerous losses and Rakhim sought to ensure that the [[Imperial Governor]] was safely extracted. He began escorting [[Elias An'Therosed|An'Therosed]], but had to leave his side to fend off the [[Brothers of Retaliation]], as they began closing in on the two. This left the Governor on his own to reach the [[Escape Pod]] chamber, but the [[Chaos Space Marine]] [[Salid]] managed to reach An'Therosed and attacked the Governor. He managed to survive Salim's blows and Rakhim attacked the Chaos Space Marine, so that the Governor could escape. However moments later, the [[Chaos]] invaders shut off power to the [[Hive-spire]]. This prevented the Escape Pod from working and left An'Therosed, Rakhim and the surviving Space Wolves stranded on [[Asedor]].{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*''Rakhim'', the [[Brothers of Retaliation]], [[Asedor]] and [[Elias An'Therosed]] were created by [[Lorens Karaca]]. They appeared in [[The Citadel Journal 33]].{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The Citadel Journal 33]], pgs. 62-67 - ''Operation Salvation''

